## Which Package Lets You Add a Stage Platform

The [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) is the one that lists it. That package, at 490 euros ex VAT, includes a 60 inch LED display, one gooseneck plus one wireless handheld microphone and a technician on site for up to 6 hours, for up to 120 guests. Modular stage platforms are on its list of optional extras at 35 euros per square meter.

None of our other packages lists a stage platform. The [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/) at 295 euros ex VAT, for up to 40 guests, includes a projector with a screen, sound and one gooseneck microphone, and its optional extra is the technician. If you want a stage with it, or with an Eco Pack, a Wedding Pack or a Product Presentation Pack, tell us and we quote it together with the package.

## Priced by the Square Meter

The MICE Pack extra is 35 euros per square meter, so you size the stage in square meters: width times depth. A stage of 4 by 2 meters is 8 square meters, which at that rate is 280 euros. That figure is the MICE Pack extra, not a published price for a platform on its own, and it is an example of the arithmetic, not a quote.

We publish no price for a platform on its own and no daily or weekly rate, so for any other booking we quote it with the rest of your event. Tell us the room, the number of speakers and the date.

## How Big a Stage Does Your Event Need?

Start from who stands on it, not from the room.

-   **One speaker at a lectern.** A small stage is enough. Leave room on the platform for the lectern and the microphone too.
-   **A panel of seated speakers.** It needs the width of the row plus space for a table and the chairs, which usually makes the stage deeper than a lectern stage.
-   **A host who walks.** The more the speaker moves, the more floor the speaker needs. If the speaker walks a stage, our guide to [wireless handheld microphone rental](/blog/wireless-handheld-microphone-rental/) explains the microphones we own.

Then check the room: the height of the ceiling, the sightlines from the back rows and where the screen goes, so the platform does not hide the slides.

## Height, Steps and Safety

We publish no height, load rating, steps, handrails, ramps or surface finish for our platforms. The inventory list shows the platforms as Guil modules of 2x1 and does not list steps, handrails or ramps as separate items.

If your venue needs a given height, access for people with reduced mobility or a safety certificate, tell us before you book. We say plainly what we can and cannot offer. Anything outside our own platforms, such as a different kind of stage, is not in our own inventory, and we look for a solution with our suppliers, if there is one. We do not promise availability or a price until we have checked.

## Stage Platforms, Sound and Technician

A stage platform is only half of a stage. The speakers need sound, and a speaker on a raised floor needs the microphone and the speaker system placed for it. Our crew delivers the platforms with the rest of the equipment, and we work delivery only, with no self pickup. We publish no setup time, because it depends on the room and the size of the stage.

The [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) includes a technician on site for up to 6 hours, who operates the sound and the microphones and solves any fault with the sound or the screen. An extra hour is 40 euros. On the Basic MICE Pack a technician is optional at 240 euros per day. The technician runs the sound, not the slides, so the speaker controls what is shown on the screen.

## How to Choose a Stage Platform Rental

Whoever you hire, these five questions are worth asking. Here are our answers:

-   **Who owns the platforms?** Modular Guil platforms are ours. Anything beyond them, or a different kind of stage, is sourced from suppliers, and we tell you so.
-   **How is it priced?** By the square meter on the MICE Pack extra, and quoted for any other booking.
-   **What are the height and the load rating?** We publish neither. Ask whoever you hire to confirm both in writing if your event needs them.
-   **Who sets up the sound?** Our crew delivers the equipment, and a technician during the event is included in the MICE Pack and optional on the Basic MICE Pack.
-   **How does it arrive?** We work delivery only, with no self pickup, and every booking needs at least 24 hours of notice.

